; The demo installs the platform the way any other product would: from a registry, as versioned
; packages. It does not reach into platform/ — that separation is the point of this directory.
;
; The @loomweaver packages are not on the public npm registry yet, so until the first public release they
; come from LoomWeaver's own feed. This file names the registry; it deliberately holds no
; credential. CI authenticates with the build identity (npmAuthenticate), and locally you supply a
; token the way your feed expects.
@loomweaver:registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/crosslabs-gmbh/_packaging/loomweaver/npm/registry/
